  ],
  "notes": "Header labels from PCB silkscreen beside each pin ('V3' as printed at the bottom-left of the header). Header housing markings '1B' and a small triangle near +5V are not labeled pin numbers, so rule 4's 2xN default was used. QWIIC (43)/(44) are GPIO numbers kept as functions. TX_1..RX_4 / IO04..IO10 and DATA/CLOCK IO8/IO3 callouts describe internal RS485/CAN and APA102 LED wiring, not header pins. 7~12V screw terminal and the four 3-pin RS485/CAN module sockets have no individual pin labels and are skipped."
